{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"356471fc695a3926","name":"card_unit_48th_armored_infantry","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/BrothersInArms/units/card_unit_48th_armored_infantry","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"48th ARMORED INFANTRY","text":"Reduce damage to this unit by 2 for each adjacent unit.","flavorText":"The 48th Armored Infantry, nicknamed “Dragoons”, was a unit of the US Army during WWII. In 1942 the regiment was assigned to the 7th Armored Division which first saw combat in France during the Normandy Campaign in June 1944. In September 1944 the division was attached to the British Second Army in the Netherlands where it fought in Operation Market Garden, which was a failed attempt to outflank the German defenses of the Siegfried line and ensure a swift advance towards Berlin. Later that year, when the division was getting ready to advance into Germany, the German Ardennes Offensive began on 16 December 1944, also known as the Battle of the Bulge. The division was then ordered to the Belgian town of St. Vith, where it managed to stall the German advance during a week of heavy fighting. Finally the 7th Armored Division was forced to withdraw, but after a brief rest it managed to recapture the town of St. Vith by 23 January 1945. In February 1945 the 7th Armored advanced into Germany and participated in fighting near the Hürtgen Forest and later during the Allied encirclement of the Ruhr Pocket. After the war ended the division served in occupation duty in Germany, but returned to New York in October 1945 where it was inactivated. Later the 1st and 2nd Battalions of 48th Infantry were later assigned to the 3rd Armored Division in West Germany during the Cold War.","faction":"USA","type":"infantry","rarity":"Rare","cost":4,"operationCost":1,"attack":5,"defense":5},"defaults":{"Name":"card_unit_48th_armored_infantry","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_48th_armored_infantry_title","SourceString":"48th ARMORED 